		(uuid "0c1efe05-ef50-48a3-89fe-ddf1ff5d9e5a")
	)
	(text "Supply: 5 V DC from a Mean Well DDR-60L-5 DIN-rail converter. The converter is not on this board. It converts and\nisolates the 48 V battery (18-75 V in, 5 V 12 A out, 4 kVdc input to output). There is no 48 V on this board.\nWiring: DDR-60L-5 +Vo (terminals 3, 4) to J6 pin 1, -Vo (terminals 1, 2) to J6 pin 2. Fuse the 48 V feed to the\nconverter separately. Board load budget: 5 A (25 W), under half of the converter's rating.\n\n5 V setting: the converter output adjusts from 4.5 V to 5.5 V. F2, Q1, Q2 and the cable drop about 0.2 V at 5 A.\n    With the board running, adjust the converter until TP14 reads 5.10 V. TP14 must stay within 4.75-5.25 V (CM5 limits).\n\nF2  5x20 mm fuse in a PCB holder (XC-7, LCSC C3131, rated 6.3 A). The fuse is fitted by hand, not by the assembler.\n    Fuse: Littelfuse 021806.3MXP (LCSC C142706): 6.3 A time-lag, glass, 7.6 mOhm. Do not fit a larger fuse: 6.3 A is\n    the holder's limit. The converter limits its output to 12.6-16.2 A (constant current), 2.0 to 2.6 times the fuse\n    rating. Into a short F2 opens slowly: within 2 minutes at 13.2 A, and it may not open at 12.6 A. The converter's\n    current limit is the short-circuit protection: size the copper from J6 through F2, Q1 and Q2 for 16 A.\nQ1  SI7137DP P-channel MOSFET (20 V, 2.5 mOhm at 4.5 V): reverse-polarity protection. With J6 pin 1 positive the body\n    diode lifts the source, the gate is at GND through SW1, and Q1 turns on. With the supply reversed the gate and\n    source are both near 0 V, so Q1 stays off and blocks: nothing reaches the board and F2 does not blow.\nQ2  Second SI7137DP, back to back with Q1 (sources joined): the on/off switch. Q1 alone cannot switch the board off,\n    because its body diode conducts. SW1 2-3 closed = ON (gates to GND). SW1 2-1 = OFF: R14 holds both gates at the\n    sources. The converter stays powered when SW1 is off. Q1 + Q2 drop about 25 mV and dissipate 0.13 W at 5 A.\n    The gates see the full input voltage: the gate rating is 12 V, and D2 clamps below that.\nD2 SMCJ6.0A 1.5 kW TVS: 6 V stand-off (above the converter's 5.5 V maximum setting), 6.67 V minimum breakdown,\n    10.3 V clamp. It absorbs cable ringing when the supply is connected live. It sits after Q1/Q2 so that a reversed\n    supply cannot forward-bias it. It cannot absorb a sustained over-voltage: the converter's own over-voltage\n    shutdown (5.75-7 V) covers that.\nC15/C16 100 uF 10 V polymer, C17-C20 10 uF: bulk capacitance of the 5V rail. They are after Q1, so a reversed\n    supply never reaches the polarized parts. The converter allows up to 6800 uF of external capacitance.\n\nJ6 pin 2 is board GND. The converter isolates it from the battery negative. GND is tied to CHASSIS on the top sheet."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 55.88 102.87 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "186ea055-1511-4795-bb7f-94b366852106")
	)
	(text "Fuse, reverse-polarity protection, on/off switch, surge clamp, bulk capacitors"
